---
description: >-
  Markdown-string labels (backtick-quoted: bold, italic) with htmlLabels: false,
  so labels fall back to the SVG-text (tspan) rendering path. Pairs with
  6-markdown-label-html-true.mmd, same label content, only htmlLabels differs.
  Under this path, bold/italic markers are stripped but the surrounding
  whitespace collapses (e.g. "bold" and "and" run together) -- a known,
  pre-existing rendering quirk of markdown labels without htmlLabels, not
  something this fixture is meant to fix.
config:
  htmlLabels: false
---
flowchart TD
  A["`This is **bold** and *italic* text`"] --> B["`A second markdown label`"]
